A pilgrimage is a gathering, and [[Org/The Harlequins/index|the Harlequins]] are known to organize them. Invitations are blue paper reading that through connections, guile, or something perhaps more unsavory, the bearer has acquired an invitation, with the rest in gold text; each invites one and names no recipient. [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs Marchal]] has been to a pilgrimage before, in [[Geography/Istria/index|Istria]]. The Party believes the gathering is connected to the six gods said to be coming to destroy [[Færrin]].

The current pilgrimage is held at [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]], a dead mining town a little under a day's drive out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. Its centerpiece is an Istrian strider under construction, a platform on eight legs with buildings on top, still ringed with scaffolding. The host and his Istrian companions are building it and call it the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], and the host means to take it on a pilgrimage to the Void Side Wall. Crossing the town line flattens every raiment to the same plain gray, so that no one can be read for the god behind their blessing.

The host is a tall lanky figure plainly not human. He wears a black pinstriped suit and a plain white mask with crescent eyes and a wide black toothless grin, and he speaks over a crowd without raising his voice. The strider cannot hold the some four hundred guests of the opening night, so a place aboard goes to whoever holds a [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystone]] when it leaves, six months after that night. He has said he will harm no one while the strider is unfinished. With a week to go, he announced that a reminder would go out to everyone originally invited, and warned of festivities on the road.

On the opening night the main street was dressed for a party: electric fairy lights on the old lamp posts, banners reading "Pilgrimage Welcome," tables of hors d'oeuvres and champagne, and hundreds of guests, some with three or four armed attendants. Guests handed in their invitations at a table and were given plain white masks, all alike, that pressed to any face and changed nothing of the wearer. Weapons were not taken from anyone. The Harlequins served drinks and hors d'oeuvres, and their platters carried a faint whiff of sulfur.

The games along the street pay in hints toward the keystones. The fortune-telling booth reads Harrow fortunes and then gives a hint. A barker before a rainbow-prism box sets seven walls of seven colors around a key, with seven potions to pass them and a riddle to work out the order. A table of dice takes a fifty-gold buy-in against a hint. A Harlequin with a painter's palette stands before blank wooden mannequins.

Two signposted paths lead out of town. The crossed-swords path leads to the disused train yard, where a Harlequin at an observation deck spins a wheel of colors and rings a bell, and creatures come out of the smoke to fight whoever goes down. Those who survive are led to a foreman's office and given three questions. The Harlequin there will not give a keystone's location, nor cross streets to it. The fairy-ring path leads to a parking lot behind a shuttered store, where a Harlequin runs an association game: three mushroom rings set in a Venn diagram, one player to each, and items to be laid in the four overlaps that connect the players. What connects them earns a soft ding; what does not brings an anvil, a pit of acid or a volley of darts.

Among the other guests are an elf and a gnome. The elf is [[Org/Protectorate/People/Tamara McKay|Tamara McKay]] of the [[Org/Protectorate/index|Protectorate]], and the two of them are after keystone 8.

The [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] has its own interest in the gathering. Its Project Entrainment means to reach the source of the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] and change what emits it, and the message the Party read about the pilgrimage was part of that project. The company's logs speak of sending its own people in among the guests.
